1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:04,036
Meet Onto. One idea today: the key.

2
00:00:04,136 --> 00:00:08,125
A key is the columns that name one row, and only one.

3
00:00:08,225 --> 00:00:12,309
For SAP order lines: client, order and item. MANDT + VBELN + POSNR.

4
00:00:12,409 --> 00:00:16,123
If a key repeats, every join on it repeats rows.

5
00:00:16,223 --> 00:00:20,837
In our SAP example, 17 of 17 keys are unique.

6
00:00:21,187 --> 00:00:24,927
Try it in your browser: krusgraph.com/check
